Z||000000||DJRice||06-05-2001||10:12 PM||||I've been wondering thru the archives in preparation for my PW,PL,PM install and I have a good set of GT doors that I intend to install on my SE, I just want to make sure this is the best way to go.  I have compiled all of the parts I need now and all I have left to do is put the final coat of paint on my mirror housings and get ahold of a door spring tool so I can go ahead and replace my hinge pins while I have things dismantled. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> <P>To those who have installed Power Windows and Locks, did you swap the whole door, or did you install the motors and hardware in your existing doors?  I have found posts indicating that people have done both, I just want to get an idea of how many people have done it each way and how things worked out.  <P>BTW, Ogre, your cave is looking good.  I hadnt checked it out since your last update.  Is it true that Ogres have layers?  <BR>(have you seen 'Shrek' yet?)<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||06-05-2001||10:30 PM||||I swapped the motors into my existing doors. I wanted to retain the VIN tags on my doors, and didn't want to have to mess with aligning the door, if it would even align. I've posted before about the mill and drill process and hinge cutouts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||06-05-2001||10:34 PM||||I too swapped out the motors etc and kept my original doors.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||06-05-2001||11:18 PM||||Just to be different I swapped the entire door- had no alignment problems.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||06-05-2001||11:33 PM||||I swapped both doors on my 84 with another 84 and had no alignment problems at all!  Didn't even have to adjust the door glass.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||06-06-2001||01:26 AM||||Motors, simple!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Galen||06-06-2001||01:51 AM||||I've swapped a door from a 87 to a 84..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> no problems<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
